1
00:04:20,571 --> 00:04:26,571
Give your soul to the dance.

2
00:08:41,142 --> 00:08:47,142
Suspiria is a horror, mystery, drama film directed by Luca Guadagnino.

3
00:13:01,714 --> 00:13:07,714
A darkness swirls at the center of a world-renowned dance company, one that will engulf the
artistic director, an ambitious young dancer, and a grieving psychotherapist.

4
00:17:22,285 --> 00:17:28,285
Some will succumb to the nightmare.

5
00:21:42,857 --> 00:21:48,857
Others will finally wake up.

6
00:26:03,428 --> 00:26:09,428
Susie, played by Dakota Johnson.

7
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Madame Blanc / Dr. Klemperer / Helena Markos, played by Tilda Swinton.

8
00:34:44,571 --> 00:34:50,571
Sara, played by Mia Goth.

9
00:39:05,142 --> 00:39:11,142
Miss Tanner, played by Angela Winkler.

10
00:43:25,714 --> 00:43:31,714
Miss Vendegast, played by Ingrid Caven.

11
00:47:46,285 --> 00:47:52,285
Patricia, played by Chloë Grace Moretz.

12
00:52:06,857 --> 00:52:12,857
Suspiria is a 2018 supernatural horror film directed by Luca Guadagnino from a screenplay by
David Kajganich, inspired by Dario Argento's 1977 Italian film of the same name.

13
00:56:27,428 --> 00:56:33,428
It stars Dakota Johnson as an American woman who enrolls at a
prestigious dance academy in Berlin run by a coven of witches.

14
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
Tilda Swinton co-stars in three roles, as the company's lead choreographer, as a male
psychotherapist involved in the academy, and as the leader of the coven.

15
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
Mia Goth, Elena Fokina and Chloë Grace Moretz appear in supporting roles as students, while Angela Winkler, Ingrid
Caven, Sylvie Testud, Renée Soutendijk and Christine LeBoutte portray some of the academy's matrons.

16
01:09:29,142 --> 01:09:35,142
Jessica Harper, star of the original film, has a cameo appearance.

17
01:13:49,714 --> 01:13:55,714
A remake of Suspiria was first announced in 2008 after Guadagnino had acquired the
rights from the original film's writers, Argento and Daria Nicolodi.

18
01:18:10,285 --> 01:18:16,285
In September 2015, Guadagnino confirmed his plans to direct, describing his version
as an "homage" to the original rather than a straightforward remake.

19
01:22:30,857 --> 01:22:36,857
A new screenplay was drafted by Kajganich, who had written
Guadagnino's A Bigger Splash the year before.

20
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
Kajganich set the film during the so-called "German Autumn" of 1977 to explore
themes of generational guilt in that country during the Cold War.

21
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
The film's other themes include motherhood, evil
and the dynamics of matriarchies.

22
01:35:32,571 --> 01:35:38,571
Unlike the original film, which used exaggerated colors, Guadagnino conceived the
visuals in Suspiria as "winterish" and bleak, absent of primary colors.

23
01:39:53,142 --> 01:39:59,142
The film incorporates stylized dance sequences choreographed by Damien
Jalet, which form part of its representation of witchcraft.

24
01:44:13,714 --> 01:44:19,714
Principal photography took place in late 2016 and early
2017 in Varese, Italy, and in Berlin.

25
01:48:34,285 --> 01:48:40,285
The musical score was composed by Radiohead singer Thom
Yorke, who took inspiration from krautrock.

26
01:52:54,857 --> 01:53:00,857
The film is dedicated to the memories of Vogue Italia editor-in-chief Franca
Sozzani, film director Jonathan Demme and Deborah Falzone.

27
01:57:15,428 --> 01:57:21,428
Suspiria premiered at the 75th Venice International
Film Festival on September 1, 2018.

28
02:01:36,000 --> 02:01:42,000
It was given a limited release by Amazon Studios in Los Angeles and New York on October 26, 2018, where it grossed
over $180,000 in its opening weekend, marking the highest screen-average box-office launch of the year.

29
02:05:56,571 --> 02:06:02,571
It was screened on October 31 in some U.S.

30
02:10:17,142 --> 02:10:23,142
cities before opening in wide release on November 2, 2018.

31
02:14:37,714 --> 02:14:43,714
It was released in Italy on January 1, 2019.

32
02:18:58,285 --> 02:19:04,285
The film was a box-office bomb and critical response was polarized; some praised the film for its visual elements and
performances, while others criticized its historical-political setting as arbitrary in relation to its other themes.

33
02:23:18,857 --> 02:23:24,857
The film explores themes of berlin, germany, dance
performance, berlin wall, telepathy, 1970s.

34
02:27:39,428 --> 02:27:45,428
The tone is emotional and dark and thought_provoking.
